Adaptogens are herbs and mushrooms traditionally used to help the body adapt to physical and emotional stress. The best known among mushrooms is Reishi, called the “mushroom of calm” in the East.

## An evening ritual in 4 steps

- 1.5 hours before bed, switch off screens or turn on night mode
- Make a tea: 1 teaspoon of lemon balm + ½ teaspoon of Reishi powder
- Drink it slowly in a quiet place — 5 minutes of deep breathing
- Go to bed at the same time every day

Lemon balm's citrusy aroma balances Reishi's bitterness, and together they make a soft, calming drink. Results are usually felt after 2–3 weeks of regular use.

> Sleep doesn't begin in bed — it begins with the first quiet minute of the evening.
